remuda: cluster call: missing SESSION for capture
Call a remote node API: list, capture, or a read-only support probe. Example: remuda cluster call <NODE> list

Usage: remuda cluster call NODE (list|capture SESSION|support) [--addr IP[:PORT]] [--json]

Arguments:
  <NODE>     Remote node id, alias or fingerprint
  <ACTION>   list, capture or support
  [SESSION]  Session to capture; required for capture

Options:
  -h, --help              Print help
      --addr <IP[:PORT]>  Address; omitted port defaults to 7441
      --json              Print results as JSON; support defines its own object

Next: remuda cluster call NODE (list|capture SESSION|support) [--addr IP[:PORT]] [--json]
